hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4621","Yusuf bin Saeed reported, saying: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Sulayman al-Ahwal told me, that Tawus told him, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by a man while he was circumambulating the Kaaba, led by a man with a prick in his nose, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, cut him off.” He greeted him with his hand, then ordered him to lead with his hand.” Ibn Jurayj said: And Suleiman told me that Tawus told him on the authority of Ibn Abbas, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a person while he was circumambulating the Kaaba, and he tied his hand to another person with a cuff, a thread, or something. Other than that, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, cut it with his hand and then said: Drive it with his hand. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4622","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, saying: Sufyan told us, saying: Ayoub told us, saying: Abu Qalaba told us, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “We do not vow to disobey God, nor do we vow to do what the son of Adam does not possess.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4623","Ishaq bin Mansour narrated, he said: Abu Al-Mughirah narrated, he said: Al-Awza’i narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Thabit bin Al-Dahhak said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam is a liar, then he is as he said, and whoever kills himself with any of This world will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection, and no man is obligated to vow that which he does not possess.”"
"4624","Yusuf bin Saeed reported, saying: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Saeed bin Abi Ayyub told me, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, he told him That Abu Al-Khair narrated to him, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, who said: “My sister vowed to walk to the House of God, so she ordered me to ask a fatwa for her. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I consulted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “You should walk and you should ride.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4625","Amr bin Ali and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Zahr, that Abu Saeed told him, on the authority of Abdullah bin Malik, that Uqba bin Amir told him: “He asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about... A sister of his vowed to walk barefoot and not veiled, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Order her to veil herself, ride, and fast three days. \days\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"4626","Bishr ibn Khalid reported, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja’far reported, on the authority of Shu’bah, saying: I heard Suleiman, who is Al-A’mash, speaking on the authority of Muslim Al-Batin, On the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “A woman boarded the sea and vowed to fast for a month, but she died before she could fast.” Then her sister came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned that to him, so he ordered her to fast on her behalf.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4627","Ali bin Hajar and Al-Harith bin Miskin reported a reading on him while I was listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: “Saad Ibn Ubadah consulted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding a vow he made to his mother. She died. Before you make it up, he said: Make it up for her.”"
"4628","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “He asked a fatwa Saad bin Ubadah, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a vow he made to his mother, and she died before she could fulfill it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Peace and blessings be upon him: Make it up for her.”"
"4629","Muhammad bin Adam and Harun bin Ishaq informed me, on the authority of Abdah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Bakr bin Wa’il, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid. Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “Saad bin Ubadah came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: My mother has died.” And she had a vow that she had not fulfilled. He said: “Fulfill it on her behalf.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4630","Ishaq bin Musa Al-Ansari reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, “that there was a night in He vowed to seclude himself from pre-Islamic times, so he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered him to seclude."
"4631","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid reported, saying: Sufyan told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “Umar bin Al-Khattab vowed to seclude one night in the Sacred Mosque, so he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered him to seclude. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4632","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam narrated, saying: Muhammad bin Jafar narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, saying: I heard Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, On the authority of Ibn Omar, “Omar had set aside a day for him to seclude himself in pre-Islamic times, so he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, and he ordered him to do so.” \to seclude\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"4633","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abdullah bin told me Ka'b bin Malik, on the authority of his father, that he said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he repented to him: “O Messenger of God, I will be freed from my wealth.” As charity to God and His Messenger, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Keep some of your money on you, for it will be better for you.” Abu Abdul Rahman told us: It appears that Al-Zuhri heard this hadith from Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik, and he heard it from Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah, on the authority of him in a long hadith"
"4634","Suleiman bin Dawud reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Yunus, saying: Ibn Shihab said, so Abd al-Rahman bin Ka’b bin Malik informed me Abdullah bin Ka'b said: I heard Ka'b bin Malik narrating his story when he lagged behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a campaign. Tabuk, he said: When I sat in front of him, I said: “O Messenger of God, part of my repentance is that I give up some of my wealth as charity to God and to His Messenger,” he said. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Hold back some of your money, for it will be better for you.” So I said: “I will keep back my share that was in Khaybar.” A summary of the hadith of repentance"
"4635","Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: Laith bin Saad told us, he said: Aqeel told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Ka'b bin Malik told me that Abdullah bin Ka'b bin Malik said: I heard Ka'b bin Malik, He recounts his story when he lagged behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the Battle of Tabuk. He said: “I said: O Messenger of God, part of my repentance is I give away some of my wealth as charity to God and to His Messenger. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Keep some of your money as a gift for you, for it will be better for you. I said: I am holding back my arrow that was at Khaybar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4636","Muhammad ibn Ma’dan ibn Isa ibn Ma’dan reported, saying: Al-Hasan ibn Ayan told us, saying: Ma’qil told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abd informed me Al-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Ka’b, on the authority of his uncle Ubaid Allah bin Ka’b, who said: I heard Abu Ka’b bin Malik speaking. He said: I said: “O Messenger of By God, my salvation is only through honesty, and it is part of my repentance that I will not tell anything except the truth as long as I remain, God willing, and it is part of my repentance that I will give up my wealth. As charity to God and to His Messenger. He said: “Keep back some of your wealth, for it will be better for you.” I said: “I am holding back my arrow that was in Khaybar. Will it enter Land is in the money if it is vowed (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4637","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik told me, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Abu al-Ghaith Salem, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Khaybar, and we did not take any spoils except wealth, belongings and clothes, so a man gave a gift.” From Banu al-Sabib, who is called Rifa`ah ibn Zayd, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has a black boy who is called Mu’adim. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to May God bless him and grant him peace until Wadi Al-Qura, until we were in Wadi Al-Qura, while an armored vehicle was landing the saddle of the Messenger of God, when an arrow came to him and struck him, killing him. So the people said: Congratulations to him in Paradise, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the shamla that he took on the Day of Khaybar Of the spoils, Al-Qasim did not reach them so that a fire would ignite on them. When the people heard that, a man brought two traps and two traps to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: One or two traps of fire."
"4638","Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sadfi reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith reported, that Kathir ibn Farqad told him: Nafi` He told them, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever swears an oath and says: God willing, will have a double.”"
"4639","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ Whoever swears an oath and says: God willing, he will make an exception. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4640","Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, saying: Affan told us, saying: Wahib told us, saying: Ayyub is Al-Sakhtiyani told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever takes an oath and says: God willing, he has the choice. If he wishes, he may go ahead, and if he wishes, he may leave it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4641","Imran bin Bakkar told us, he said: Ali bin Ayyash told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Abu Al-Zannad told me, from what Abd al-Rahman al-Araj told him, What he mentioned is that he heard Abu Hurairah narrating it on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “And Suleiman bin Dawud said: I will surround Tonight, ninety women, all of them will bring a knight who fights in the cause of God. His companion said to him: Say: God willing. He did not say: If he wills. By God, He went around all of them, and only one of them became pregnant, and she came with the half of a man. I would love the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad if he had said: If God wills, they will strive in the cause of God all together as knights.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4642","Ahmad bin Yahya bin Al-Wazir bin Sulaiman and Al-Harith bin Miskin reported a reading to him, while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Ka’b bin Alqamah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Shamasa, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, that the Messenger of God prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The expiation for a vow is the expiation for an oath.”"
"4643","I am Suwaid bin Nasr. He said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak informed us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, “that he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about hunting, and he said: When you send your dog, mention the name of God over it, and if you catch it and it is not killed, then slaughter it. And mention the name of God over it. If you find that he has been killed and has not eaten, then eat. He has kept it from you, but if you find that he has eaten from it, then do not eat. If your dog mixes with dogs and they kill and do not eat, then do not eat any of it, for you do not know. \You killed\"""""""
"4644","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, he said: “I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, about hunting of prey, and he said: Whatever you catch with its animal, eat it, and whatever you catch with its prey is safe, and I asked him about the dog, So he said: If you send your dog and he takes it and does not eat, then eat, then if he takes it, then it is due for it, but if there is another dog with your dog and you fear that it might be He was taken with him and killed, so do not eat, for you only named your dog and did not name anyone else.”"
"4645","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Abu Abd al-Samad Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Samad al-Ammi told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Adi ibn Hatim, “He asked the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: Send the teaching dog.” So he takes it? He said: If you send the trained dog and mention the name of God over it and it takes it, I said: And if it kills? He said: And if it kills, I said: Throw it away Regarding the symptom, he said: If its part is affected, then eat, and if its part is affected, then do not eat."
"4646","Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Muhammad al-Kufi al-Muharbi told me, he said: Abdullah bin al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Haywa bin Shurayh, he said: I heard Rabia bin Yazid, saying: Abu Idris told us, God forbid, he said: I heard Abu Thalabah Al-Khushani, saying: “I said: O Messenger By God, I am in a hunting ground. I hunt with my bow, and I hunt with my trained dog, and with my dog, which is not trained. So he said: You did not hit your bow, so remember. The name of God be upon him and eat, and whatever you strike with your dog that is a teacher, mention the name of God and eat, and whatever you strike with your dog that is not a teacher, then you realize His intelligence, so eat.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4647","Muhammad ibn Zanbour Abu Salih al-Makki informed us, saying: Fudayl ibn Iyadh narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, said: “I said: O Messenger of God, shall I send my marking dogs, and they will stop me and I will eat?” He said: If you send your dogs The teacher, so hold on to you, then eat. I said: Even if they kill. He said: Even if they kill. He said: Unless a dog from other than them joins them. I said: Throw away? And if it breaks, then eat, but if it hits the part of it, then do not eat.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4648","Amr bin Yahya bin Al-Harith told me, he said: Ahmad bin Abi Shuaib told us, he said: Musa bin Ayan told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Asim Ibn Sulaiman, on the authority of Amer Al-Shabi, on the authority of Adi Ibn Hatim, “He asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about hunting, and he said: If you send Your dog mixed with a dog that you did not use the name of, so do not eat it, for you do not know which one killed him.”"
"4649","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Zakaria told us, and he is Ibn Abi Zaida, he said: Amer told us, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, He said: “I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the dog, and he said: If you send your dog and name it, then eat, and if you find another dog with Do not eat your dog, for you only named your dog and did not name anyone else.”"
"4650","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: Muhammad, who is Ibn Ja`far, told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, He said: Al-Sha’bi told us, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, who was our neighbor and foreigner and connected to the two rivers, that he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: I sent my dog, and I found with my dog a dog that was taken, and I do not know which one was taken. He said: Do not eat, for you only named your dog and did not name anyone else.” Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: He told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Udayy. On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similar to this (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4651","Sulayman bin Ubayd Allah bin Amr Al-Ghaylani Al-Basri told us, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Abdullah bin told us Abi Al-Safar, on the authority of Amer Al-Shabi, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, who said: “I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I said: Send my dog. He said: If You sent your dog and named it, “Kul,” and if he ate from it, do not eat, for he only kept it for himself. And if you sent your dog, you found it with him. “Anything other than it, so do not eat, for you only named your dog and did not name anything else.”"
"4652","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Al-Safar, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, On the authority of Sa`id ibn Masruq, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Adi ibn Hatim, he said: “I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I will send my dog and find There was another dog with my dog. I don’t know which one he took. He said, “Do not eat. You only named your dog and did not name anyone else.”"
"4653","Ahmad bin Suleiman informed us, he said: Yazid, who is the son of Harun, informed us, he said: Zakaria and Asim informed us, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Adi. Ibn Hatim, he said: “I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about hunting that is hunted, and he said: Whatever catches its limit then eat it, and whatever catches its incident He is stubborn. He said: I asked him about the hunting dog, and he said: If you send your dog and mention the name of God, then eat. I said: And if it kills, he said: And if he kills him, then if he eats from it, do not eat. If you find a dog with him other than your dog and he killed it, do not eat, for you only mentioned the name of God. May God Almighty bless your dog and do not mention anything other than him.”"
"4654","Amr bin Yahya bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Ahmad bin Abi Shuaib told us, he said: Musa bin Ayan told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Asim Ibn Sulaiman, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Adi Ibn Hatim Al-Tai, “He asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about hunting and said: If you send “Your dog and you mentioned the name of God over it, and it killed it and did not eat, then eat it. But if it eats some of it, do not eat it. He only kept it for himself and did not eat it for you.”"
"4655","Kathir bin Ubaid told us, he said: Muhammad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Ibn Al-Sabbaq told me, he said: You told me Maimuna, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Gabriel, peace be upon him, said to him: But we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or a picture.” So it became. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on that day would order the killing of dogs. He would even order the killing of a small dog.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4656","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the killing of dogs.” “Except what is excluded from it.”"
"4657","Wahb bin Bayan Al-Masry told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, he said: Ibn Shihab said, Salem told me Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of his father, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raising his voice “ordering the killing of the dogs,” and the dogs were \It shall not be killed except a hunting dog or livestock.\"""""""
"4658","Qutaibah told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the killing of dogs except A hunting dog or a livestock dog.”"
"4659","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If dogs were not one of the nations, I would have ordered them to be killed. “They took a dog that is not a dog for plowing, hunting, or livestock, for it will detract from its reward every day by a Qirat.”"
"4660","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, and Yahya bin Saeed told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mudrik, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, On the authority of Abdullah bin Naji, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Angels do not enter a house in which \A picture"","" nor a word"","" nor a form.\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"4661","Qutayba bin Saeed and Ishaq bin Mansour informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abu Talha, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image.”"
"4662","Muhammad bin Khalid bin Khalili told us, he said: Bishr bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Ibn al-Sabbaq told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Maimuna, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, informed me, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, arrived one fine day. Maimuna said to him: Messenger of God, I have disapproved of your appearance since today. He said: Gabriel, peace be upon him, promised me that he would meet me. Tonight, he did not meet me. By God, he did not leave me alone. He said: And his day continued like that, then a puppy dog fell on himself under our table. So he ordered him to be brought out, then he took water in his hand and sprinkled it on his place. When evening came, Gabriel, may God bless him and grant him peace, met him, and the Messenger of God said to him: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: You promised me that you would meet me yesterday. He said: Yes, but we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or a picture. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the morning of that day, he ordered the killing of the dogs. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4663","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he heard him say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he said: “Whoever catches a wild dog or a livestock dog, two qirats will be deducted from his reward every day.”"
"4664","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said “Whoever keeps a dog, other than a hunting or livestock dog, two qirats will be deducted from his reward every day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4665","Suwayd bin Nasr bin Suwayd informed us, he said: Abdullah, who is Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us on the authority of Hanzalah, he said: I heard Salim narrate On the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever keeps a dog, his reward will be reduced by two qirats every day, unless it is a wild animal or a dog. \cattle owner\"""""""
"4666","Ali ibn Hajar ibn Iyas ibn Muqatil ibn Mishmraj ibn Khalid al-Saadi informed us, on the authority of Ismail, who is ibn Ja`far, on the authority of Yazid He is Ibn Khusayfa. He said: Al-Sa’ib ibn Yazid informed me that Sufyan ibn Abi Zuhair Al-Shinai’i came to them, and he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever keeps a dog that is not sufficient for his crops or udder, one qirat of his work will be deducted from his work every day.” I said: O Sufyan, you Did you hear this from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, by the Lord of this mosque."
"4667","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya, Ibn Abi Adi, and Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Mughaffal, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever keeps a dog, other than a hunting dog, or a livestock or agricultural dog, his reward will be reduced every day.” carat (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4668","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever keeps a dog, other than a hunting, agricultural or livestock dog, his work will be reduced every day.” carat"
"4669","Wahb bin Bayan told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, he said: Ibn Shihab told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever keeps a dog is not a hunting dog, nor is it a possession of livestock or land. For two Qirats are reduced from his reward every day.”"
"4670","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, meaning Ibn Jafar, he said: Muhammad bin Abi Harmala told us, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, On the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever keeps a dog, other than a livestock dog or a hunting dog, his work will be reduced every day.” A carat.” Abdullah said: Abu Hurairah said: Or a plowing dog. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4671","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham, He heard Abu Masoud Uqba say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the price of a prostitute.” \the priest\"""""""
"4672","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Marouf bin Suwayd al-Jadhami informed us, that Ali bin Rabah Al-Lakhmi narrated to him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not permissible for the price of a dog, nor for the priest’s clothing, nor for \The prostitute's dowry\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"4673","Shuaib bin Yusuf informed us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yusuf, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The worst of earnings are the dowry of a transgressor, the price of a dog, and the earnings of a cupper.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4674","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan Al-Maqsimi told me, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the price of cats and dogs, except for hunting dogs.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: The hadith of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, is not authentic. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4675","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Ibn Sawa told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Abu Malik, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, “A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I have dogs that are hounds, so give me fatwa about them. He said: What has happened to you?” Your dogs, then eat. I said: Even if they kill. He said: Even if they kill. He said: Give me a fatwa regarding my bow. He said: If your arrow returns to you, then eat. He said: Even if it disappears. Ali? He said: And if something disappears on you and you do not find any traces of an arrow other than your own on it, or you find that it has dried up, meaning it has become stank. Ibn Sawa said: I heard it from Abu Malik Ubayd Allah bin Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God grant him peace and blessings (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4676","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Saeed bin Masruq, on the authority of Abaya bin Rifa’ah bin Rafi’, on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij, who said: “While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Dhul-Hulayfah of Tihama, they attacked camels. And sheep, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in the last of the people. The first of them hastened, so they slaughtered and set up pots, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave them to them. God, peace and blessings be upon him, ordered the pots to be poured out, and they were filled in full. Then he divided among them, and he equated ten sheep to a camel. There were only a few horses among the people, so they chased him and he made them weak. Then a man shot him with an arrow and God imprisoned him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed “These beasts have creatures like the creatures of wild beasts, so whatever of them overwhelms you, do likewise to them.”"
"4677","Ahmad ibn Mani` told us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak told us, he said: Asim al-Ahwal informed me, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Adi ibn Hatim. He said: “I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about hunting, and he said: When you shoot your arrow, mention the name of God Almighty, for if you find it, you have He is killed, then eat unless you find him falling into water, and you do not know whether the water killed him or your arrow.”"
"4678","Amr bin Yahya bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Ahmad bin Abi Shuaib told us, he said: Musa bin Ayan told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Asim Ibn Sulaiman, on the authority of Amer Al-Shabi, on the authority of Adi Ibn Hatim, “He asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about hunting, and he said: If you send Your arrow and your dog, and you mentioned the name of God, so he killed your arrow and eat. He said: So if he stays away from me for a night, O Messenger of God? He said: If I find your arrow and why? If you find traces of something other than that in it, eat, but if it falls into water, do not eat.”"
"4679","Ziyad bin Ayyub informed us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr informed us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, he said: “ I said: O Messenger of God, we are people of hunting, and one of us shoots game and misses it for a night or two, so he seeks the trail. Then he finds him dead and his arrow is in him. He said: If you find the arrow in him but do not find any traces of a snake on him, and you know that your arrow killed him, then eat."
"4680","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala and Ismail bin Masoud told us, saying: Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you saw your arrow in it but did not see any trace of it and knew that it was \He killed him and he ate\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"4681","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Maysara, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, On the authority of Adi bin Hatim, he said: “I said: O Messenger of God, shoot the game and look for its trace after a night. He said: If you find your arrow in it and do not Seven eat from it, then eat.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4682","Ahmad bin Khaled Al-Khallal told me, he said: Ma’an told us, he said: Mu’awiyah, who was Ibn Salih, told us, and he mentioned a word that means, about Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Tha’labah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “about the one who catches his catch after Three, let him eat it unless it stinks.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4683","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, he said: I heard Murri bin Qatari, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim He said: “I said: O Messenger of God, I send my dog, and he takes the game, but I cannot find anything to kill him with, so I kill him with a shovel and a stick.” He said: Spill blood as you wish, and mention the name of God Almighty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4684","Muhammad ibn Qudamah told me, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Adi ibn Hatim, he said: “I said: Oh Messenger of God, I send the trained dogs, and they catch me. Shall I eat from it? He said: If you send the trained dogs and mention the name of God? So they caught you and eat. I said: Even if they kill. He said: Even if they kill, as long as a dog that is not one of them does not engage it. I said: And I shoot game. He said: “If you throw something with the meat, and it hits it, then eat. If it hits the meat, then do not eat.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4685","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar told us, on the authority of Al-Shu’abi, He said: I heard Adi bin Hatim, he said: “I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about turning away, and he said: If he does the right thing, then eat, and then “If it harms its body and kills it, then it is disgusting, so do not eat it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4686","Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Dhara’ told us, he said: Abu Muhsin told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, he said: “ I asked the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about prepared game, and he said: If it tastes fresh, eat it, and if it tastes fresh, do not eat it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4687","Ali ibn Hajar informed us, he said: Issa ibn Yunus and others informed us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Adi ibn Hatim, he said: “ “I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about wild game, and he said: Whatever you catch with its animal, eat it, and whatever its prey catches, it is safe.”"
"4688","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdul Rahman informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Musa, and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna informed us, On the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of Wahb ibn Munabbih, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever lives in the desert is dry, whoever follows hunting is heedless, and whoever follows the ruler will be tempted.” And the wording is by Ibn Al-Muthanna. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4689","Muhammad bin Muammar Al-Bahrani told us, he said: Hibban, who is Ibn Hilal, told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “A Bedouin came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a rabbit that he had roasted, so he placed it In his hands, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, held back and did not eat, and he ordered the people to eat, but the Bedouin held back, so the Prophet said to him, “Pray May God bless him and grant him peace: What prevents you from eating? He said: I fast three days of every month. He said: If you are fasting, then fast during the day. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4690","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hakim bin Jubayr, Amr bin Uthman, and Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of Ibn al-Hutakiyya, said: Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: “Who will be present with us on the day of the battle?” He said: Abu Dharr said: I will come The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, brought a rabbit, and the man who brought it said: I saw it bleeding. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was eating, then He said: Eat. A man said: I am fasting. He said: What is your fast? He said: Three days of every month. He said: Where are you regarding the bad eggs? Thirteen, fourteen and fifteen? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4691","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hisham, who is Ibn Zayd, he said: I heard Anas, saying: “ We produced a rabbit with the bitter gourd of Dhahran, so I took it and brought it to Abu Talha. He slaughtered it, and he sent me with its thighs and hips to the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he accepted it.”"
"4692","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, and Daoud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Safwan, he said: “I shot two rabbits. I did not find anything with which to slaughter them, so I slaughtered them with bitterness, so I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, and he ordered me to eat them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4693","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, While he was on the pulpit, he saluted, he was asked about the lizard, and he said: “I do not eat it, nor do I prohibit it.”"
"4694","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, and Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that a man said: O Messenger of God What do you see in the fog? He said: “I neither eat it nor do I prohibit it.”"
"4695","Kathir ibn Ubaid informed us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Harb, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, he said: Al-Zuhri informed me, on the authority of Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Abbas, on the authority of Khaled bin Al-Walid, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought to a roasted lizard. It was approached and it fell in love.” With his hand to eat from it, those who were present said to him: O Messenger of God, it is lizard meat. So he removed his hand from it, and Khaled bin Al-Walid said to him: O Messenger of God, is the lizard forbidden? He said: No, but it is not in the land of my people, so I find myself abstaining from it. So Khaled fell in love with the lizard, so he and the Messenger of God ate some of it. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is watching.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4696","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he informed him, that Khalid ibn al-Walid informed him, “He entered with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on Maimuna bint Al-Harith, who was his maternal aunt. So the meat of a lizard was presented to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not He eats something until he knows what it is. Some of the women said: Will you not tell the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, what he eats? I told him that Lizard meat, so he left it. Khaled said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is it forbidden? He said: No, but it is food that is not in the land of my people. Then I found that he spared it.” Khalid said: “I brought it back to me and I ate it while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked on.” Ibn al-Asam told him, on the authority of Maymouna, and he was in her lap"
"4697","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “My aunt gave a gift to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, aqat, ghee and a lizard. He ate some of the aqat and the ghee and left He was filthy and ate at the table of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Even if it had been forbidden, he would not have eaten at the table of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. \And he greeted\"""""""
"4698","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr informed us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “that He was asked about eating ghee, and he said: Umm Hufaid presented to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ghee, and pure ghee, and ghee, and he ate some of the ghee. And the one who picks, and leaves the fog, detests them, and if it were forbidden, they would not have been eaten at the table of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, nor did he order their eating.”"
"4699","Suleiman bin Mansour Al-Balkhi told us, saying: Abu Al-Ahwas Salam bin Sulaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahb, on the authority of Thabit bin Yazid Al-Ansari said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on a journey, and we stayed at a certain place, and a fog engulfed the people. So I took a lizard and roasted it, then brought it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he took a stick with which he counted his fingers and then said: A nation of Bani Israel has transformed into animals on earth, and I do not know which animals they are. I said: O Messenger of God, the people have eaten from them. He said: What is our command? By eating it and not forbidding it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4700","Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Bahz bin Asad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Adi bin Thabit told me, he said: I heard Zaid bin Wahb narrates, on the authority of Thabit bin Wadi’ah, who said: “A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a lizard, and he began to look at it and turn it over.” He said: “A nation has been transformed and it is not known what it did, and I do not know whether this is one of them.”"
"4701","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahb, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, on the authority of Thabit bin Wadi’ah, “A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a lizard and said, ‘A nation has been transformed, and God knows best.’” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4702","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ammar, he said: “I asked Jabir bin Abdullah about the hyena and he ordered me to eat it. I said: Is it hunting? He said: Yes. I said: I heard it from the Messenger of God.” God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Yes? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4703","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Hakim, on the authority of Ubaida bin Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every wild animal with fangs is forbidden to eat.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4704","Ishaq bin Mansour and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Idris, on the authority of Abu Tha’labah Al-Khushani, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the eating of any wild animal with fangs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4705","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir told us, he said: Baqiyyah told us, on the authority of Buhair, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Ubayy Alopecia, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The plundering animal is not permissible, nor is it permissible for any wild animal that has fangs, nor is it permissible for one that crouches.”"
"4706","Qutaibah and Ahmad bin Abdah told us, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Amr, who is Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of Jabir, He said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade and mentioned, on the Day of Khaybar, the meat of donkeys and the call to prayer for horses.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4707","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fed us meat horses, and forbade us from the meat of donkeys.”"
"4708","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Al-Hussein, who is Ibn Waqid, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, On the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fed us On the Day of Khaybar, he permitted the meat of horses, and forbade us from the meat of donkeys.”"
"4709","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ubayd Allah, who is Ibn Amr, told us, he said: Abdul Karim told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “We were We eat horse meat at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"4710","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Baqiya bin Al-Walid told us, he said: Thawr bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Salih bin Yahya bin Al-Miqdam bin Ma’di Yakrib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Khalid bin Al-Walid, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “It is not permissible to eat the meat of horses, mules, and donkeys.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The one before this hadith is more correct than this hadith. It is as if it is true, if it is true, to be abrogated, because his saying: permission to eat horse meat is evidence of that."
"4711","Kathir ibn Ubaid told us, he said: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Thawr ibn Yazid, on the authority of Salih ibn Yahya ibn al-Miqdam ibn Ma’di Yakrib. On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Khalid ibn al-Walid, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade eating the meat of horses and mules. And donkeys, and every wild animal with fangs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4712","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “We were We eat horse meat. I said: mules. He said: No? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4713","Muhammad bin Mansour and Al-Harith bin Miskin informed us of a recitation of it while I was listening and its pronunciation, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muhammad and Abdullah bin Muhammad, on the authority of their father, said: Ali said to Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him “And he forbade temporary sexual intercourse and the meat of private donkeys on the Day of Khaybar.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4714","Abu Dawud Sulaiman bin Dawud told us, he said: Abdullah bin Wahb told us, he said: Yunus, Malik, and Usama told me, about Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Abdullah, my son Muhammad ibn Ali, on the authority of their father, on the authority of Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, who said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade women’s sexual intercourse on the Day of Khaybar, and the meat of female donkeys.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4715","Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr informed us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Omar informed us, and Amr bin Ali, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the meat of donkeys.” Civility on the Day of Khaybar.” Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ubaid informed us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, and Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, is similar, but he did not say: Khaybar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4716","Muhammad bin Abdul Ala told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: “He forbade The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the Day of Khaybar gave information about the meat of female donkeys, both mature and raw.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4717","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi He more fully said: “On the day of Khaybar, we caught a donkey coming out of the village, and we cooked it, and the herald of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called out: Indeed, the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He has forbidden the meat of donkeys, so fill the pots with what is in them, so We have had enough of them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4718","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, 27 on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Messenger of God has risen in the morning.” May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Khaybar, so they came out to us with the wipers. When they saw us, they said: Muhammad and Al-Khamis, and they returned to the fort running, so he raised The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his hands, then said: God is great, God is great. Khaybar was ruined. When we camped in a people’s square, it was ruined. It was the morning of those who had been warned, so we poured some red meat in it and cooked it. Then a herald called out to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Indeed, God Almighty and His Messenger He forbids you from donkey meat, for it is an abomination.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4719","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir bin Dinar informed us, saying: Baqiyya informed us, on the authority of Buhair, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Abu Tha’labah Al-Khushani, that he told them, “They invaded with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Khaybar.” The people were hungry, so they found therein donkeys of human donkeys, so the people slaughtered some of them. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was informed of that, so Abdul ordered Al-Rahman bin Awf then announced to the people: “The meat of human donkeys is not permissible for one who bears witness that I am the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4720","Amr bin Othman bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Baqiya, he said: Al-Zubaidi told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abu Alopecia Al-Khushani, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the eating of any wild animal with fangs, and the meat of domestic donkeys.”"
"4721","Qutaibah told us, he said: Our favorite narration is Ibn Fadala al-Masri, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “ On the Day of Khaybar, we ate the meat of horses and wild animals, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from eating donkeys. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4722","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Bakr, who is Ibn Mudar, told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Had, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Isa bin Talha On the authority of Umayr bin Salama al-Dhamri, he said: “While we were walking with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with some of the souls’ belongings while they were in a state of sanctuary, when A wild, beheaded donkey. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Leave him, for his owner is about to come to him. Then a man from Bahz came, who is the one who He licked the donkey and said: O Messenger of God, what about this donkey? So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered Abu Bakr to divide it among the people. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4723","Muhammad bin Wahb told us, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahim told me, he said: Zaid bin Abi Unaisah told me, on the authority of Abi Hazim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, Abi Qatada, said: “It struck a wild donkey, and its companions brought it while they were in a state of ihram. It is lawful, so we ate from it, and some of us said to one another, “If we had asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about it, we would have asked him,” and he would have said: “It is lawful.” You did well, so he said to us: Do you have any of it? We said: Yes. He said: Give us some of it. So we brought some of it to him and he ate from it while he was in Ihram. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4724","Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Makki told us, he said: Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, he said: Ayyub told us, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Zuhdum, “that Abu Musa brought a chicken, and a man from the people stepped aside and said: What is the matter with you? He said: I saw it eating something dirty, so I swore not to eat it? Then Abu Musa said, “Eat and eat, for I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, eating it, and he commanded him to atone for his oath.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4725","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Al-Qasim Al-Tamimi, on the authority of Zuhd Al-Jarmi, he said: “We were with Abu Musa So he brought food, and in his food he offered chicken meat, and among the people was a man from Banu Taim Allah who turned red as if he were a servant, but he did not approach, so Abu said to him “Moses approached, for I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, eating from it.”"
"4726","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid al-Muqri informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Suhayb, the client of Ibn Amir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No human being kills a sparrow, or anything above it, unlawfully, except God Almighty asked him about it. It was said: O Messenger of God, and what is the right to it? He said: He should slaughter it and eat it and not cut off its head and throw it away. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4727","Ismail bin Masoud told us, on the authority of Bishr, who is Ibn al-Mufaddal, he said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of Ali bin al-Hakam, on the authority of Maymun bin Mahran. On the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade on the Day of Khaybar the eating of anyone with a claw of birds, and every wild animal with fangs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4728","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Sa`id bin Salamah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Abi Burdah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “In sea water is what is pure, its water is permissible for its dead.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4729","Muhammad bin Adam Al-Masisi told us, he said: Abdah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Wahb bin Kaysan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, He said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent us three hundred of us, carrying our provisions on our necks. Then we increased our provisions until a man had all of us.” On the day of a date, it was said to him: O Abu Abdullah, where did the man find the date? He said: We found it but lost it when we lost it, so we came back? The sea, and behold, a whale had been thrown up by the sea, so we ate from it for eighteen days.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4730","Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Makki told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, who said: I heard Jabir, saying: “We sent the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him Three hundred riders greeted our emir, Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah. We were watching the caravan of Quraysh. We stayed on the coast, and we were struck by severe hunger until we ate. The knocking, he said: Then the sea gave us an animal called the amberjack, so we ate from it for half a month and it lubricated us from its mound and our bodies were firm. And Abu Ubaidah took one of his ribs and looked at the tallest camel and the tallest man in the army, so he passed under him. Then they became hungry, so he slaughtered a man. Three islands, then they were hungry, so a man slaughtered three islands, then they were hungry, so a man slaughtered three islands, then Abu Ubaidah forbade it. Sufyan said: He said: Abu Al-Zubair: On the authority of Jabir. We asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Do you have any of it? He said: So we took out such-and-such from his eyes? Likewise, a small group of people from Wadak, and four people came to Hajjaj, and Abu Ubaidah had a bag of dates in it, and he used to give us the handful, then he went on. To the date, and when we lost it, we found it lost.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4731","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr told us, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “We sent the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace We were with Abu Ubaidah in a company. We ran out of supplies and passed by a whale that had been thrown into the sea. We wanted to eat from it, but Abu Ubaidah forbade us. Then He said: We are messengers of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and in the path of God, eat, and we ate from it for several days. When we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, We told him, and he said: If there is anything left with you, send it to us.”"
"4732","Muhammad bin Omar bin Ali bin Muqaddim Al-Muqaddami told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent us with Abu Ubaidah, and we were three hundred and twelve, and he provided us with a sack of dates. So he gave us a fistful of it, and when we rewarded him, he gave us one date after another, so that we could suck it as a child sucks, and drink water from it. And when we lost it, we found that we had lost it, to the point that we would bang it with our bows and blow it up, then drink of the water over it, until we were called an army. Then we crossed the coast, and suddenly there was an animal like a dungeon called amber. Abu Ubaidah said: Dead meat, do not eat it. Then he said : The army of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and in the cause of God Almighty, and we are forced to eat in the name of God, so we ate from it and made from it. And there were thirteen men sitting in the same place. He said: Then Abu Ubaidah took one of his ribs and took the body of a camel out of it. He drove the people away and passed under it. When we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: What kept you prisoner? We said: We were following the caravans of Quraysh We mentioned to him the matter of the animal, and he said: That is a provision that God Almighty has bestowed on you. Have you gained any of it? He said: We said: Yes. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4733","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Saeed bin Khalid, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Uthman, “A doctor mentioned a frog in medicine at the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but the Messenger forbade it.” May God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"4734","Humayd ibn Masada al-Basri informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, who is Ibn Habib, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Abu Ya`four, that Abdullah ibn Abu Awfa said: “We fought seven battles with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we were eating locusts.”"
"4735","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan, who is Ibn Uyaynah, told us, on the authority of Abu Yafour, he said: “I asked Abdullah bin Abi Awfa, Concerning the locusts, he said: I fought six battles with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. We eat locusts. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4736","Wahb bin Bayan told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa’id, and Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “An ant bit one of the prophets, so he ordered the village of ants to be destroyed, and it was burned. Then God Almighty revealed to him: “If an ant has bitten you, you will have destroyed a nation among the nations that glorified God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4737","Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Al-Nadr, who is Ibn Shumail, informed us, he said: Ash’ath informed us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, “A Prophet descended One of the prophets was under a tree, and an ant stung him, so he ordered their house to be burned along with everything in it, so God revealed to him: Is there just one ant? Al-Ash’ath said: On the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he added, “They praise God.” Ishaq told us. Bin Ibrahim, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, something similar, but he did not narrate it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4738","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Laith told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Haad, on the authority of Omar bin Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Saeed bin Murjanah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever frees a believing slave, God will free every limb of him from Hell.” \Until his chastity is freed by his chastity.\"""""""
"4739","Mujahid bin Musa told us, he said: Makki bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Hakim, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Murjanah said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever frees a believing slave, God will free all “An assortment of it, an assortment of it from the Fire, so much so that God frees the hand with the hand, and with relief the relief.”"
"4740","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdullah bin Saeed bin Abi Hind told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Hakim. On the authority of Sa`id bin Murjanah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Any Muslim man frees a Muslim woman, Its redemption was from the fire, every part of it being replaced by another part of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4741","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abu Nu’aym, he said: Al-Hakam bin Al-An’am told us, he said: Fatima bint Ali told me, she said: he My father: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever frees a soul, God will protect him with every part of him, a part of the fire.”"
"4742","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: a Kufi sheikh called Shu’bah told us, he said: I was with Abu Burdah bin Abi. Moses, and he said to his sons Abdullah, Bilal, and others: O my sons, shall I not tell you a story that my father told me, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? And peace be upon him? They said: Yes, he said: “Whoever, meaning: frees a slave, God will free every part of him from the place of Hell.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4743","Ismail bin Masoud told us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: Hisham told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Salim bin Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ma’dan bin Abu Talha, on the authority of Abu Najih, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Any man who frees a Muslim man, God will He makes a shield for each of his bones a bone from the bones of him who freed him from the fire. And if a Muslim woman frees a Muslim woman, then God will make the protection of every bone of hers a bone of hers that freed her from the fire.”"
"4744","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Jaad, he said: I narrated on the authority of Ka’b bin Al-Bahzi once said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Which night do I hear?” He said: The middle of the last night. He said: And he used to say: Any Muslim man who frees a Muslim man, he will be redeemed from the Fire, and every bone of him will be rewarded for his bone. A Muslim woman, and He will redeem her from the Fire; every bone of her is a bone of hers.”"
"4745","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told me, he said: Yahya bin Adam told me, he said: Favorable narration, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ka'b ibn Murrah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Any Muslim man frees another Muslim man, his redemption from the Fire will be great.” With a bone, and any Muslim man who frees two Muslim women will be redeemed from the Fire, two bones from it for a bone. And any woman “If a Muslim woman frees a Muslim woman, then she will be redeemed from the Fire, bone for bone.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4746","Muhammad ibn Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem ibn Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ka’b ibn Murrah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever frees a slave, that will be his redemption from the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4747","Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Shurahbil bin Al-Samat, he said: We said to Ka’b bin Murrah, tell us on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and beware. He said: I heard the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever frees a Muslim man, his redemption from the Fire will be rewarded, every bone for one bone being replaced. “Two Muslim women were redeemed from the Fire, and the place of each of their bones was replaced by a bone of its own.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4748","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Khalid, meaning Ibn Zayd, Aba Abdul-Rahman al-Shami, speaking about Shurahbil bin Al-Samat, on the authority of Amr bin Abasa, said: I said to him: O Amr bin Abasa, relate to us a hadith that you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever frees a Muslim slave, the ransom for every limb of him shall be ransomed.” from the fire of hell” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4749","Amr bin Othman told me, he said: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Safwan, he said: Sulaym bin Amir told me, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Al-Samat, that he said To Amr bin Absa: Narrate to us a hadith that you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever frees a believing slave, his redemption from the Fire will be made, limb by limb.”"
"4750","Saeed bin Omar Al-Homsi told us, he said: Baqiya told us, he said: Hariz told us, he said: I heard Sulaym bin Amir, narrating the hadith of Sharhabeel bin Al-Samit, When he said to Amr bin Absa, “Tell us a hadith, in which there is no addition or subtraction.” Amr said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever frees a previously faithful slave, he will be redeemed from the Fire, limb by limb.”"
"4751","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Tamim Al-Masisi told me, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Hariz bin Uthman, on the authority of Sulaym bin Amer. Al-Khabayri, on the authority of Amr bin Absa, that he was with Sharhabeel bin Al-Samat, who is the governor of Homs, and he said: O Amr bin Absa, He told us on the authority of the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a hadith in which there was no omission or forgetfulness. He said: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Amr ibn Absa, “there is no “A man frees a Muslim slave, except that every part of him will be sacrificed for a part of him from the Fire.” I have heard it more than once. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4752","Muhammad bin Ibrahim, called Ibn Sadran Basri, told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: I read to Abd al-Hamid bin Jafar. On the authority of Al-Aswad bin Al-Ala, on the authority of a servant of Suleiman bin Abdul-Malik, that Omar bin Abdul-Aziz sent a message to a man from the Levant, So he told him two hadiths in one evening, and he said: How did you tell me about Al-Sanabihi? He said: Al-Sanabihi told me that he met Amr bin Absa, and he said: Is there a hadith in which there is no addition or subtraction? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever frees a slave, God will free every limb from Hell.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4753","Yazid bin Sinan told us, he said: Abdullah bin Hamran told us, he said: I am Abdul Hamid bin Jafar, he said: Al-Aswad bin Al-Ala informed me. Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Hawwi, the client of Suleiman bin Abdul-Malik, that Omar bin Abdul-Aziz sent a message to a man from the Levant and spoke to him. Two hadiths in the evening, then he said: How is the hadith that you told me on the authority of Al-Sanabihi? He said: I am Al-Sanabihi, he met Amr ibn Absa, and he said: Is there a hadith on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in which there is no addition or Decrease? He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever frees a slave, God will free every member of it from the Fire.”"
"4754","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am Malik bin Mihran al-Dimashqi, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abi Abla, on the authority of a man, he said: We told Wathilah He told us a conversation in which there was neither addition nor subtraction, so he became angry and said: One of you hangs the Qur’an in his house and looks at it at both ends of the day, and he does not He memorized the surah. He said: Then he went to the people and spoke to them. He said: So I said to him, “Speak to us, may God forgive you.” He said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” In the Battle of Tabuk, a group of Banu Sulaym came and said: O Messenger of God, our companion has made it obligatory. He said: So he should be freed. neck, for every limb has a limb of fire.”"
"4755","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid, the Meccan reciter, informed us. He said: Ubayy told us. He said: Ibn al-Mubarak told us. He said: Ibrahim bin Abi told us. Abla, on the authority of Al-Gharif ibn Ayyash, on the authority of Wathilah ibn Al-Asqa’, said: A group of Banu Sulaym came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: “Indeed A friend of ours made it obligatory. He said: Let him free a slave, and God will redeem every part of him from the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4756","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman, the companion of Al-Shafi’i, told us, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, he said: Abdullah bin Salem told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Abu Abla, he said: I was sitting when Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’ passed by, leaning on Abdullah bin Al-Daylami. He paused and then came to me and said: It is strange that the Sheikh did not speak to me, meaning: Wathila. I said: What happened to you? He said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the Battle of Tabuk, when a group of Banu Sulaym came to him and said: O Messenger of God, “Our companion has... He obliged, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Free a slave on his behalf. God will free each of his limbs from the Fire. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4757","He said: Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Habiba, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one who is freed at death is like the one who is guided after he is satisfied.”"
"4758","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Abu Marawahih, that Abu Dharr told him, He said: O Messenger of God, “Which work is best?” He said: Belief in God and jihad in His cause. He said: And which slaves are best? He said: It is the most expensive in price, and its soul is with its people.”"
"4759","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam informed us, saying: Ubayy told us, and Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Ja`far, he said: Urwa told me, on the authority of Abu Marawahih, on the authority of Abu Dharr, that he asked the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Which deed is best?” He said: Faith in God and jihad in the path of God. He said: Which slaves are better? He said: They are the most expensive in price and the cheapest with their owners. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4760","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “No son repays his father unless he finds him owned, buys him, and frees him.”"
"4761","Issa bin Muhammad Abu Umair Al-Ramli, and Issa bin Yunus is known as Al-Fakhouri, told us on the authority of Damra, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin A dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever owns a mahram relative will be freed.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said to us: No. We know that someone narrated this hadith on the authority of Sufyan without a dhamma, and it is an objectionable hadith, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4762","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, and Abu Dawud told us, Hammad told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever owns a mahram is free.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4763","Suleiman bin Ubayd Allah Al-Basri informed us, he said: Bahz, he said: I am Hammad, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever owns a mahram is free.”"
"4764","Muhammad bin Hatim Al-Marwazi told us, he said: I am Habban, he said: I am Abdullah, he said: I am Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, On the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever owns a mahram is free.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4765","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Hammad told us, he said: I Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Whoever owns a mahram is free.”"
"4766","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bakr told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim al-Ahwal and Qatada, then he mentioned A word that means on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever owns a mahram of a relative, he is free.” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"4767","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Abd al-Ala, then he mentioned a word that means: Sa`id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Omar ibn al-Khattab, He said: “Whoever owns a relative of a mahram, he is free,” and Qatada used to take him seriously. On the authority of Qatada, that Al-Hasan and Jabir bin Zayd said: “Whoever has a kinship will be free.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4768","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, he said: Omar said: “Whoever has a kinship, he is free.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4769","Amr bin Ali and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, saying: Abdul Rahman told us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Al-Hakam, that Omar He said: “Whoever owns a relative of a mahram, he is free.” The wording is from Amr. Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, who said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of al-Hakam, who said: Omar said: . . . . The same as him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4770","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of al-Hakam, he said: Omar said: “Who is the king of a merciful person? \He is free.\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"4771","Amr bin Ali and Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, saying: Abu Asim told us, saying: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: Omar said: “Whoever possesses a mahram or a mahram relative, he is free.” Amr bin Ali told us, he said: I heard Abu Al-Walid, says: I saw in the book of Abu Awanah, narrated by Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Omar L5913, similar to it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4772","Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Yazid Al-Dunni. On the authority of Maimuna, the mistress of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked “about the child of adultery.” He said: “There is no good in him. I strive hard.” Or he said: “I will be provided with them, which is dearer to me than freeing the child of illegitimate.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4773","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I heard Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Nabit bin Shait, on the authority of Jaban, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “No one who is disobedient or disobedient will enter Paradise.” “Not the child of adultery, nor one who is addicted to alcohol.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4774","Amr bin Ali told me, he said: Yahya told me, he said: Sufyan told me, he said: Mansour told me, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Jaban, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “No one who is disobedient, nor one who is immoral, nor one addicted to alcohol, nor one born of adultery will enter Paradise.” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"4775","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Jaban, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “No one who is addicted to alcohol, nor one who is immoral, nor one who is disobedient to his parents, nor one born of adultery will enter Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4776","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, that Abdullah said: “ “No adulterer, no one who disobeys his parents, no one born of adultery will enter Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4777","Amr bin Uthman told me, he said: Baqiya told us, he said: Shu`bah told me, he said: Yazid bin Abi Ziyad told me, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “No immoral person, no rebellious person, nor the child of adultery will enter Paradise.” Zaida disagreed with him, and said: On the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, and Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, and he did not mention in it: The son of an adulteress. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4778","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar Al-Kufi told us, he said: Al-Hussein told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’ad and Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one who is addicted to alcohol, nor an adulterer, nor an adulterer will enter Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4779","Malik bin Saad Basri told us, he said: Ruh told us, he said: Attab bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Khusayf, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “No one who is addicted to alcohol, no one who is disobedient, or one who is immoral will enter Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4780","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ya’la told us, he said: Musa, who is al-Juhani, told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah, he said: “Four people will not enter Paradise: a disobedient to his parents, an alcoholic, an adulterer, and the child of adultery.” It was narrated by Abd al-Karim, On the authority of Mujahid, he said: He substituted “the apostate as a Bedouin after immigration” instead of fornication."
"4781","Wasil bin Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “The child of an adulteress will not enter Paradise.”"
"4782","Abdul Rahman bin Ibrahim Duhaim Al-Dimashqi told us, he said: Marwan bin Muawiyah Al-Fazari told us, he said: Al-Hasan told us, he said: I heard Mujahid, He said: I was staying with Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Saeed bin Abi Dhubab in Medina, and he delayed one night, then he came to us while he was He says: Abu Hurairah distracted me from you. An outcast whose mother has bereaved me. If what Abu Hurairah said is true, then I said: And what did Abu Hurairah tell you? He said: He told us tonight on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, two hadiths: As for one of them, he claimed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “The child of adultery will not enter Paradise.”"
"4783","Muhammad bin Wahb bin Abi Karimah Al-Harrani told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahim told us, he said: Zaid told me, On the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhubab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, Mujahid said: I was camping with Ibn Abi Dhubab. So I heard him say: God has disgraced an outcast if Abu Hurairah was truthful. The outcast has perished if Abu Hurairah was truthful. Abu Hurairah claimed that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “A child born of adultery will not enter Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4784","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, “He was descending upon a servant God has a boy with him who is called an outcast. He said: Your mother has bereaved you. He is an outcast, if Abu Hurairah is telling the truth. Mujahid said to him: What is that? He said: He says: “No child born of adultery will enter Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4785","Ahmad bin Saeed informed me. He said: Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah told us, who is Ibn Saad al-Dashtaki. He said: Amr told us, who is Ibn Abi Qais. On the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No “The child of adultery, and none of his descendants through seven fathers, will enter Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
